newest release in CHANGELOG.md. GitHub records this repository's parent as
go-gitea/gitea, and the upstream history is present in full — the history root
is Gogs' first commit (475e3471b4, 2014-02-11, Joe Chen) and the top ten
authors by commit count are all upstream maintainers. The rebrand begins at
61fc4c7183 (2026-07-15).

Gitea is itself a fork of Gogs, and both copyrights are retained in LICENSE:

    Copyright (c) 2015 The Gogs Authors

Upstream Gitea ships no NOTICE file. MIT has no NOTICE mechanism; it requires
the copyright notice and permission text to be retained, which LICENSE and the
per-file headers do.

FILE HEADERS

Commit edb3cec504 added "Copyright 2026 Hanzo AI, Inc." above the existing
notices in 2978 files. Upstream's lines were retained, not replaced — MIT
requires it, and the attribution is true. Nothing named "The Git Authors" was
introduced: Git is a different project under a different licence, and putting
its name on this code would attribute it to people with no connection to it.

